                                                "sense_id": "a81b3dd0-6887-3d72-b34c-ddf204ae9e20",
                                                "text": "When the chief has directed them to approach, they advance; those who have the calumets, chant and dance with much agility, now turning around each other, and now presenting themselves in front, but always with violent movements and extraordinary contortions."
